__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
# pip-managed project (pip install -e ".[dev]"); a uv.lock is only ever a
# stray artifact of running uv here, never committed.
uv.lock
# EXCEPT a core template's own lock, which is project SOURCE (SPEC PY-16): each
# template folder declares its environment in a pyproject.toml, and shipping the
# resolved lock beside it is what stops a released build resolving against PyPI
# the first time anyone renders that template. Committed, and shipped in the
# wheel — hatchling excludes gitignored files, so without this negation the lock
# would silently not be packaged.
!fused_render/templates/*/uv.lock
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
scripts/vendor-codemirror/node_modules/
scripts/vendor-sci/node_modules/
scripts/vendor-three/node_modules/
.claude/worktrees/
frontend/node_modules/
fused_render/static/shell-dist/
# The package-level skills/ (the user-level skill sync's wheel source, D185)
# is a build-time copy of the canonical repo skills/ (D106, same pattern as
# shell-dist); never committed, shipped via `artifacts`.
fused_render/skills/
fused_render/_baked_branch.py
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
# Runtime sidecar written next to an opened file: the server writes `<file>.json`
# beside ANY file you open, whatever its extension (bookmark/session/comment
# state — e.g. learn/index.html.json, ARCHITECTURE.md.json). It is per-machine
# state and never source: a committed one hijacks the default view for everyone,
# because an empty-query open restores its `lastSession` (ARCHITECTURE.md.json
# was committed by accident and pinned the doc to one machine's git-mode
# session). The rule was `*.html.json` only, so every other extension slipped
# through. Listed per extension rather than as a `*.*.json` wildcard, which would
# also swallow genuine configs (tsconfig.build.json, settings.local.json, …) —
# add extensions here as they come up; nothing tracked has ever matched these.
*.html.json
*.md.json
*.markdown.json
*.py.json
*.txt.json

# cmux browser/screenshot captures — local scratch, never committed
cmux-assets/

# dev.sh's staged builtin-mount zips (learn.zip / sessions.zip) — build
# artifacts, freshly rebuilt on every dev.sh run, never committed
.dev-zips/
docs/superpowers/plans/
